# A file whose bytes matter keeps LF on every platform, whatever core.autocrlf says.
# Git for Windows sets it to true, and then a checkout writes CRLF.
#   *.jsonl  test data that a test reads byte for byte (the test of the Auto corpus checks for LF)
#   *.sh     bash cannot run a script that has CRLF (a Windows checkout can be used from WSL)
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
